# Rest Services Guide

A quick reference for **repositories and web service **

---

## 1. Repository Structure

```ts
import { HttpClient } from '@angular/common/http';
import { inject, Injectable } from '@angular/core';
import { getMutations, getResource, SignalGet } from 'app/core/services/rest-api';
import { Customer, CustomerRequest } from '../models/customer';

@Injectable({ providedIn: 'root' })
export class CustomerRepository {
  private readonly httpClient = inject(HttpClient);
  private readonly baseUrl = 'samples/customers.json';

  public mutations() { /* see below */ }
  public find(): SignalGet<string, Customer> { /* see below */ }
  public findBy(): SignalGet<void, Customer[]> { /* see below */ }
}

## 2. Mutations (POST, PUT, DELETE)

Use getMutations to handle create/update/delete operations with automatic signals for submitting and error.

```ts
const mutations = customerRepository.mutations();

// Create
mutations.create({ name: 'Juan', email: 'juan@example.com' })
  .then(result => console.log('Created:', result));

// Update
mutations.update({ id: 123, name: 'Juan Updated' })
  .then(result => console.log('Updated:', result));

// Signals
mutations.submitting(); // true if any mutation is running
mutations.error();      // error message if any

## 3. Single Resource (GET by ID)

Use getResource to fetch a single entity reactively.

```ts
const customerResource = customerRepo.find();

customerResource.load('123').then(customer => {
  console.log('Customer:', customer);
});

// Reactive signals
customerResource.value();   // current value
customerResource.loading(); // loading state
customerResource.error();   // error message
customerResource.destroy(); // cleanup

## 4. Resource List (GET all or filtered)

```ts
const customers = customerRepo.findBy();

customers.load().then(list => console.log('Customers list:', list));

// Signals
customers.value();
customers.loading();
customers.error();
customers.destroy();

## 5. Best Practices

- One repository per entity: CustomerRepository, OrderRepository, etc.
- Always use getMutations for write operations.
- Always use getResource for read operations.
- Signals are read-only outside the repository.
- Use destroy() in components to prevent memory leaks.
- MessageService handles errors automatically.